Z||000000||Springtyme||10-16-2001||10:43 AM||||Okay, maybe I know nothing... and someone please correct me if I'm wrong.<P>I'm searchin around Ebay, got a decal for my windhsield and trying to find something else to spend my money on and I came across a few things...<P><BR> <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=1015447654" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=1015447654</A> <P>Now, I dont know about this. I don't understand it, but as far as I know, there was no 1983 Fiero.<P><BR> <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=596605558&r=0&t=0" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=596605558&r=0&t=0</A> <P>Aren't these regular coupe wheels? <P> <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=1649027217" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=1649027217</A> <P>Well, this is a classic. 1982 Fiero matchbox car. Sure would love to see one of these... <P><BR>As I said.. maybe I know nothing...<P>*edited to add more things i find along the way*<p>[This message has been edited by Springtyme (edited 10-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||10-16-2001||10:55 AM||||The first Fiero was sold in summer/fall of 83. Hence, the 83 College football schedule. (Was for 83-84 school year.)<P>The first GT was an 85 notchback. It came with those wheels.<P>As for the 83 Hot Wheels? I haven't a clue.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"><P>Good eye, though!<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
